judge_payload.judge_prompt:
You are a senior software architect evaluating the quality of a requirements specification produced by an AI coding agent.

## Context
The agent was given this input (a vague business requirement):
<input>
{
  "role": "Product Manager",
  "requirement_description": "We need to let brands create campaigns on our platform. Brands should be able to post a brief describing what kind of content they want from creators, set a budget, and define who can apply. Once posted, creators can see the campaign in a marketplace. We already have a user system with brands and creators. This is the first version so don't overcomplicate things, but it should be production-ready. Target launch: 4 weeks.",
  "context": "The system is a FastAPI microservice called campaign-service. We have existing User and Content services. Tech stack: Python, PostgreSQL, Redis, Celery."
}
</input>

The agent produced this requirements specification:
<output>
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "document_metadata": {
    "title": "Campaign Service V1 - Technical Requirements & Specification",
    "service_name": "campaign-service",
    "author": "Staff / Senior Software Engineer",
    "target_audience": ["Product Management", "Backend Engineering", "QA", "Frontend Engineering"],
    "target_timeline": "4 Weeks",
    "tech_stack": {
      "framework": "Python 3.11+ / FastAPI",
      "primary_database": "PostgreSQL 15+",
      "cache_and_broker": "Redis 7+",
      "task_queue": "Celery 5.3+"
    },
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "executive_summary": "Requirements specification for the initial release (V1 MVP) of campaign-service. Enables brands to author, budget, target, and publish marketing campaigns, while enabling creators to discover campaigns via a high-performance marketplace feed. Architecture prioritizes simplicity, idempotency, strict state transitions, and modular integration with existing User and Content services within a 4-week delivery window.",
  "clarifying_questions_and_assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "CQ-001",
      "topic": "Escrow & Budget Lock Enforcement",
      "question": "Does campaign-service need to hold, lock, or interface with a payment/escrow service upon publishing, or is budget purely informational for V1?",
      "impact": "If financial escrow is required in V1, payment gateway integration and distributed transaction handling (Saga/2PC) will jeopardize the 4-week delivery target.",
      "default_assumption_v1": "Informational budget only. Campaign-service enforces schema validation (positive integer in cents, currency ISO-4217), but does not process real-time credit cards or fund holds. A dedicated Billing/Escrow integration hook is deferred to V1.1.",
      "rationale": "Keeps V1 scope focused on marketplace discovery while maintaining a production-ready schema that can link to payment transactions later via `payment_status` metadata."
    },
    {
      "id": "CQ-002",
      "topic": "Creator Application Workflow Scope",
      "question": "Does this microservice manage creator applications and content submissions, or does it strictly serve campaign authoring and marketplace discovery?",
      "impact": "Including application workflows, reviews, and asset upload pipelines doubles the scope of the microservice.",
      "default_assumption_v1": "campaign-service owns Campaign CRUD, State Lifecycle, Eligibility Rules, and Marketplace Search/Read endpoints. Applications and content deliverables will be handled by a dedicated `application-service` or separate Phase 2 module, linking via `campaign_id`.",
      "rationale": "Adheres to Single Responsibility Principle and ensures campaign discovery is shipped and load-tested within 4 weeks."
