    {
      "id": "CQ-003",
      "topic": "Eligibility Evaluation: Server-Side vs. Client-Side",
      "question": "Should the marketplace feed strictly filter out campaigns for which a creator is ineligible, or show all campaigns with an eligibility match badge?",
      "impact": "Strict feed filtering requires synchronous creator profile lookups or fan-out indexing per creator attribute, adding latency and tight coupling to User Service.",
      "default_assumption_v1": "The marketplace feed displays all ACTIVE campaigns by default (with optional category/budget filters). When an authenticated creator retrieves campaign details (`GET /campaigns/{id}`), the service evaluates the creator's claims against `eligibility_criteria` and returns a computed `is_eligible` boolean flag along with an array of unmet criteria.",
      "rationale": "Significantly improves marketplace browsing performance, enables public/shared caching in Redis, and prevents creator frustration caused by an empty feed."
    },
    {
      "id": "CQ-004",
      "topic": "Post-Publish Editing Rules",
      "question": "Can a brand modify campaign budget, eligibility criteria, or deadline after the campaign has been published to the marketplace?",
      "impact": "Unrestricted edits while creators are actively viewing or preparing proposals can cause bait-and-switch vulnerabilities and race conditions.",
      "default_assumption_v1": "Immutable core fields upon publication: `total_budget`, `currency`, and `eligibility_criteria` cannot be modified once the state transitions to `ACTIVE`. Brands may only edit descriptive fields (`title`, `brief_description`, `cover_image_url`) or increase the budget. To make breaking changes, the brand must cancel and create a new campaign.",
